  "description": "Compute self-attention splitting hidden dimension into multiple parallel attention heads.\n\nMulti-head attention enables representations to jointly attend to information from different representation subspaces at different positions.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\n\\text{head}_i = \\text{Softmax}\\left(\\frac{\\mathbf{Q}_i \\mathbf{K}_i^T}{\\sqrt{d_k}}\\right) \\mathbf{V}_i\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Reshape token representations into num_heads subspace partitions\n2. Compute scaled dot-product attention per head\n3. Concatenate heads back into original hidden dimension D and round to 4 decimal places\n\n### Returns\nNested 2D list of shape (N, D) representing contextualized multi-head output.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Multi-Head Attention\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nNatural language consists of discrete words and symbols arranged in sequential order. To process text with neural networks, we convert words into continuous embedding vectors and model their grammatical and semantic relationships. **Multi-Head Attention** is a core sequence-processing mechanism used in modern Transformer and LLM architectures.\n\nMulti-head attention enables representations to jointly attend to information from different representation subspaces at different positions. In this problem, the goal is to: compute self-attention splitting hidden dimension into multiple parallel attention heads.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\n\\text{head}_i = \\text{Softmax}\\left(\\frac{\\mathbf{Q}_i \\mathbf{K}_i^T}{\\sqrt{d_k}}\\right) \\mathbf{V}_i\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Reshape token representations into num_heads subspace partitions\n2. **Phase 2**: Compute scaled dot-product attention per head\n3. **Phase 3**: Concatenate heads back into original hidden dimension D and round to 4 decimal places\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Self-Attention Mechanics**: Scaled dot-product attention computes all-to-all token interactions dynamically, allowing tokens to gather context from the entire sentence simultaneously.\n* **Position Encodings**: Because self-attention is permutation-invariant, positional encodings (like sinusoidal or Rotary Position Embeddings) inject word order into the representations.\n* **Vocabulary & Subwords**: Algorithms like BPE tokenize text into frequent subwords, allowing models to represent rare words without requiring an infinite vocabulary.",
  "examples": [
