  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Multi-Head Attention** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport torch, math\n\ndef pytorch_multi_head_attention(x: list, num_heads: int = 2) -> list:\n    t = torch.tensor(x, dtype=torch.float32)\n    N, D = t.shape\n    dk = D // num_heads\n    q = t.view(N, num_heads, dk).transpose(0, 1)\n    attn = torch.softmax(torch.matmul(q, q.transpose(-2, -1)) / math.sqrt(dk), dim=-1)\n    return torch.round(torch.matmul(attn, q).transpose(0, 1).contiguous().view(N, D), decimals=4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
